' World-space (x/z, no y - guards stay on the ground plane) point a GuardPlacement's
' `patrolTo` targets.
interface GuardPatrolTarget
  x as float
  z as float
end interface

' A single Guard placement consumed by WorldRoom.addGuards(). `patrolTo`/`patrolSpeed`
' are only meaningful (and only ever set) together - invalid `patrolTo` means stand idle
' instead of patrolling (see Guard.bs).
interface GuardPlacement
  x as float
  z as float
  rotY as float
  patrolTo as GuardPatrolTarget
  patrolSpeed as float
end interface

' Fixed placements for Guard entities in WorldRoom - arbitrary spots near the map's
' center clearing, chosen so the free-fly camera can reach and orbit each one easily
' while verifying DrawableOrientedSprite's angle-bucket switching (issue #104).
' The first Guard patrols back and forth between its spot and `patrolTo` (see
' Guard.bs) at `patrolSpeed` world units/sec, playing its walk animation while it
' does - the other two just stand idle.
function getGuardPlacements() as GuardPlacement[]
  return [
    {x: 0.0, z: 0.0, rotY: 0.0, patrolTo: {x: 0.0, z: 40.0}, patrolSpeed: 15.0}
    ' {x: 60.0, z: 40.0, rotY: 90.0}
    ' {x: -60.0, z: 40.0, rotY: 180.0}
  ]
end function
